# Public README Scope

- Treat the root `README.md` as the public introduction and user-facing guide
  for installing, configuring, and using the PAIR app.
- Update `README.md` when public app behavior, supported user workflows, or
  user-facing terminology changes.
- Do not add implementation notes, internal plans, backend update procedures,
  test commands, build details, release operations, or troubleshooting dumps.
  Put those in the appropriate focused file under `docs/`.
- Update an existing canonical document instead of duplicating information.
- If no suitable document exists, create a focused document under `docs/`.
- Keep README additions concise, verified against the current UI, and useful to
  someone evaluating or operating PAIR.
